    known = {
      "Gen1Recomp 0.2.20 is the latest source-audited release. Its 6-commit / 26-file delta strengthens in-process game/Save Editor teardown and adds label-keyed Gold/Silver ROM text without changing Mod API 2, Nuzlocke hook contracts, Save Schema 4, or the supported engine range; exact-edition runtime smoke remains required.",
      "2.6.92 adds an explicit legacy mod_Compat Beta_26 compatibility alias while preserving nuzlocke_compat API 32 as the preferred modern provider/capability surface. Runtime interoperability confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.90 is a compatibility-only randomizer closure pass: active Item Randomizer visible-pickup ownership is source-confirmed, generic field_item_randomizer_provider delegation is supported, and DEV REPORT exposes starter/encounter/field-item/learnset external ownership; Randomizer Phase E remains paused/not started.",
      "2.6.89 completes Phase D implementation through item 11: Field Items explicitly normalize R/B/Y GEN1_FLAT versus Gold/Silver GEN2_POCKETS over shared data.items, Randomizer Info gains spoiler-aware read-only Field Item diagnostics through Compatibility API 32, and further randomizer implementation phases are intentionally paused with Phase B/C/D item-12 runtime certification deferred.",
      "2.6.88 adds ALLOW/DIVERSE/UNIQUE Field Item repetition control, deterministic native source-ordinal placement for UNIQUE, separate repeat-policy mapping rows, and explicit visible-vs-hidden ownership that leaves hidden/BG-event items unchanged; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.87 adds semantic Field Item categories, hard allowed/forbidden source-category constraints, and CHAOS/CATEGORY/BALANCED Field Item Balance while keeping CHAOS as the 2.6.86-compatible default; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.86 begins Phase D: visible Field Items now use the shared hard-safety candidate engine, persist by permanent edition/source identity independent of authored contents while preserving historical Randomizer-v1 seed input, and use one fail-closed key/HM/progression/story/provider protection classifier; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.85 completes Phase C implementation through item 11: Area Split toggles reproject logical encounter/tracker identity without rerolling physical randomized tables, Encounter Randomizer Info gains spoiler-aware read-only source/candidate/protection/split/fallback diagnostics, Compatibility API is 31, and live Encounter Repeats/Diversity Strength changes now reapply the encounter registry; runtime certification is deferred.",
      "2.6.84 adds configurable DIVERSE encounter strength, explicit land/cave/Surf/fishing/Headbutt/contest/roamer and Gen 2 time-bucket classification, and fail-closed preservation of static/fixed/story/progression/quest/gift/trainer/roamer encounter records; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.83 adds group-local Encounter Repeats (ALLOW/DIVERSE/UNIQUE), strengthens SIM BST/EVO/BALANCED fallback, and adds native-level/evolution-family progression-aware encounter selection under an encounter-only ep2 policy namespace; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.82 begins Random Encounter Phase C migration: shared hard-safety/soft-preference candidate resolution, canonical map/source/method/table/slot/path persistence identity, and complete sorted work-plan generation while preserving the historical Randomizer v1 encounter RNG slot; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.81 adds isolated pre-selection Starter Rerolls, spoiler-aware read-only starter diagnostics under Randomizer Info, Compatibility API 30 starter-information registry methods, and Yellow non-Pikachu starter progression hardening for the Cerulean Bulbasaur happiness gate; runtime confirmation is deferred.",
      "2.6.75 hardens randomizer stream isolation and persistent source mappings without expanding randomizer scope; existing seeded behavior is intended to remain stable and runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.66 added gameplay transaction interruption/exactly-once infrastructure plus central SafeInstall, Hook Registry, and Feature Health diagnostics.",
      "2.6.56 certifies source compatibility with Gen1Recomp 0.2.19 after its Gen 2 battle/EXP, Bill's PC, SaveData, Loader/Gen2Compat, inventory, overworld, and import changes. Protected Nuzlocke PC/Party Size/progression-lock wrappers require no migration; exact 0.2.19 runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.55 added semantic enforcement coverage and behavior-level regression gates; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.52 Kanto Reforged 1.3.0 compatibility profile and Gold restored-content pass; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.51 Kanto Reforged encounter/static/randomizer interoperability; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.50 held-item capability generalization; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.49 custom Day Care interoperability repair; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.46 adds the The World 5.10.0 compatibility profile on top of generic battle-role, expanded-metadata, and acquisition/encounter interoperability; runtime confirmation remains required.",
      "2.6.41 adds audited VanillaPlus 0.3.0 compatibility: three exact capture-required story encounters are registered as progression-required fixed/non-randomizable sources, incidental encounters remain ordinary, and Random Starter warns about VanillaPlus EVENT_CHOSE_* branching; combination runtime confirmation is required.",
      "2.6.40 fixes general interoperability correctness: PC Catches now requires explicit progression metadata for every eligible denial reason, movement assists preserve already-accelerated downstream timing, Rival classification no longer matches arbitrary custom trainer ids by substring, and Permadeath reasserts marked-dead HP at battle start; runtime confirmation is required.",
      "2.6.39 repairs release integrity without changing gameplay: executable/manifest/parent provenance now agrees, the Late Runtime forwarding closure is below the compiler hard ceiling, public-document version drift is consolidated, and Release Safety validates current top-version plus exact parent/package provenance; existing 2.6.38 runtime-test debt remains unchanged.",
      "2.6.38 fixes five correctness/safety issues: Gen 2 Rage boosts no longer count as setup, capture/acquisition policy errors fail closed, migration-error safe-stop propagates to extracted mutation modules, Sleep Clause provenance resets across Rest/new sleep episodes, and the missing 2.6.35 README history is restored; exact-edition runtime confirmation is required.",
      "2.6.37 fixes four battle-classifier correctness bugs: R/B/Y Burn Ban preserves Fire defrost, Gen 2 No Setup Moves is restricted to move-origin boosts, Gen 2 Other Stat Drops covers move-origin self drops such as Curse Speed, and Mirror Coat is classified Special under the optional Physical/Special Split; exact-edition runtime confirmation is required.",
      "2.6.35 fixes two recent-change regressions: classic R/B/Y Catch Info uses the drawable native <PK><MN> ligatures, and battle-clause installation explicitly retires stale pre-2.6.34 Accuracy wrappers before installing the independent Accuracy Drops owner on retained-module reloads; exact-edition runtime confirmation is required.",
      "2.6.33 introduced classic R/B/Y NUZ INFO Catch-page PKMN/ENC. spacing; 2.6.35 corrects the PKMN direct-font token to drawable <PK><MN>; 2.6.36 then fixes the remaining classic NEW GAME Setup header overlap and lower help-pane border intrusion; gameplay and APIs are unchanged.",
